# The insert mode, undo and the dot repeat.

=== i inserts and Esc goes back one
text:
a|bc
keys: iXY<Esc>
want:
aX|Ybc
mode: vim/normal

=== a appends after the cursor
text:
a|bc
keys: aX<Esc>
want:
ab|Xc

=== A and I
text:
  |abc
keys: AX<Esc>IY<Esc>
want:
  |YabcX

=== o and O open lines
text:
|one
two
keys: onew<Esc>
want:
one
ne|w
two

=== O opens above
text:
one
|two
keys: Onew<Esc>
want:
one
ne|w
two

=== a count repeats the text
text:
|x
keys: 3ia<Esc>
want:
aa|ax

=== 3o opens three lines
text:
|one
keys: 3ox<Esc>
want:
one
x
x
|x

=== Enter and backspace in the insert mode
text:
|abc
keys: Iab<BS><CR><Esc>
want:
a
|abc

=== insert mode stays until Esc
text:
|abc
keys: ix
want:
x|abc
mode: vim/insert

=== u undoes an insert as one step
text:
|abc
keys: ifoo bar<Esc>u
want:
|abc

=== u and Ctrl-r
text:
|one two
keys: dwdwu<C-r>
want:
|

=== dot repeats a delete
text:
|a b c d
keys: dw..
want:
|d

=== dot repeats an insert
text:
|x
keys: ia<Esc>.
want:
|aax

=== dot repeats a change at the cursor
text:
|foo foo foo
keys: cwbar<Esc>w.
want:
bar ba|r foo

=== dot with a count
text:
|abcdef
keys: x3.
want:
|ef

=== dot repeats o
text:
|one
keys: otwo<Esc>.
want:
one
two
tw|o

=== dot repeats a put
text:
|a
keys: yl..
want:
|a

=== dot repeats dd
text:
|1
2
3
4
keys: dd.
want:
|3
4

=== C changes to the end
text:
ab|cdef
keys: CX<Esc>
want:
ab|X

=== s and S
text:
|abc
keys: sX<Esc>
want:
|Xbc

=== S changes the line
text:
  |abc
next
keys: Snew<Esc>
want:
ne|w
next

=== <C-r> puts a register's text as typed
text:
|hello
keys: yiwA <C-r>"<Esc>
want:
hello hell|o

=== <C-r> with a named register
text:
|abc
keys: "ayiwo<C-r>a!<Esc>
want:
abc
abc|!

=== <C-r> of lines brings their line break
text:
|one
keys: yyA<C-r>0x<Esc>
want:
oneone
|x

=== what <C-r> put repeats with .
text:
|ab
cd
keys: yiwjA<C-r>0<Esc>.
want:
ab
cdaba|b

=== <C-r> reads the clipboard
text:
|x
clipboard: CLIP
keys: A<C-r>+<Esc>
want:
xCLI|P

=== <C-r><Esc> puts nothing
text:
|x
keys: i<C-r><Esc>y<Esc>
want:
|yx
